    "explanation": "The mole is the chemist's counting unit: 1 mol = 6.022 × 10²³ particles (Avogadro's number). Molar mass M (g/mol) is found from the periodic table. Key formulas: n = m/M (moles from mass), n = cV (moles from concentration and volume in dm³), n = N/NA (moles from number of particles). In balanced equations, coefficients give mole ratios. The limiting reagent is used up first and determines how much product forms.",
